<title>JAPAN: Kyocera extends gains as high-tech laggard.</title>
<headline>Kyocera extends gains as high-tech laggard.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Kyocera Corporation continued to rise on Thursday morning, as the ceramic package maker attracted investors as a laggard issue in the high-technology sector, traders said.</p>
<p>At 0032 GMT, Kyocera was up 100 yen at 9,210. Turnover was 432,500 shares.  </p>
<p>&quot;Kyocera has gained a reputation as a promising issue. It also attracted investors as a leading issue among manufacturers of electronic components,&quot; said a broker at a &quot;Big Four&quot; securities house.</p>
</text>
